# Operating Systems (OS)

## Definition
- Core software between users, applications, and hardware
- Manages system resources and operations

## Layers of OS
- User → Application → OS → Hardware
- OS acts as the resource manager

## Privilege Levels
- Kernel Space: Full access to hardware
- User Space: Limited access (uses system calls)

## Core Responsibilities
 
### Process Management
- Runs and schedules programs 

### Memory Management
- Allocates RAM to processes

### File System Management
- Manages files and directories

### I/O Management
- Controls input/output devices

### Device Management
- Handles drivers and hardware interaction

## Security Functions
- Authentication: Login verification
- Permissions: Access control
- Isolation: Processes separated from each other

# System Interfaces

## GUI (Graphical User Interface)
- Visual interface (icons, windows)

## CLI (Command Line Interface)
- Text-based commands

# Types of Operating Systems
- Desktop: Windows, macOS, Linux
- Server: Backend systems
- Mobile: Android, iOS
- Embedded: IoT devices
- Cloud/VM: Virtual systems

# Key Concepts

## System Protection
- Prevents unauthorized access

## Internet Connection
- OS connects and manages networks

## OS as Resource Manager
- Allocates CPU, memory, devices

## Multi-user OS
- Different users can use system simultaneously

